**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, `BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests`

**How to implement.** The three crystal-parameter records move ahead of the material library, so that a material version can hold one of them as its physics (.spec-md §3.16 'A material version can hold one of the three parameter records as its physics (S11)'; the S11.1 brief 'Material physics form'). `MaterialEntry` is declared in `MaterialLibrary.fs`, which `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` compiles long before `MuellerInverse.fs`, where the records live today (`MuellerInverse.fs:UniaxialParameters`, `:TriclinicParameters`, `:AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`), so the records and the builders S10.1 put on them (steps 332-334, `opticalProperties`) move. This departs from .spec-md §3.16's location for the builders ('promoted into `MuellerInverse.fs` as members of their parameter records'), and the departure is recorded here: §3.16's own next bullet needs the records before `MaterialLibrary.fs`, and ONE implementation of each builder still exists. This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'): after the step each record and each builder is declared once. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs`, `module CrystalPhysics` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `DispersionModels.fs` and before `MaterialLibrary.fs`: one `<Compile Include="CrystalPhysics.fs" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: the crystal-parameter records a material version can hold as its physics, each with its engine builder (spec 0050 S11.1, .spec-md §3.16). It opens what the moved bodies read (the engine's `Fields`, `MaterialProperties` and `OpticalProperties.Active`, as `MuellerInverse.fs` opens them). It holds `UniaxialParameters`, `TriclinicParameters` and `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters` in that order, each with its doc, its fields and its `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` exactly as steps 332-334 leave them. `MuellerObservation`, declared between two of them today, stays in `MuellerInverse.fs`. (2) Each record's `axes` stays in `MuellerInverse.fs`, because `ParameterAxis` is declared there and `ParameterName` in `ItemModels.fs` (step 205), both after `MaterialLibrary.fs`: directly after `ParameterAxis`, three type extensions `type UniaxialParameters with static member axes : ParameterAxis<UniaxialParameters> list = …`, the same for `TriclinicParameters` and `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`, each with the doc and the body it has today. Every `UniaxialParameters.axes` call therefore reads as today wherever `MuellerInverse` is open. `MuellerInverse.fs` opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics`, and its module doc's sentence that each parameter record carries its crystal class's builder (step 332) adds that the records live in `CrystalPhysics` (spec 0050 S11.1). No other line of the file changes. (3) The files that name a record open `OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics` where the compiler asks and change nothing else: `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs`, `LangasiteInverseTests.fs`, `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs` and `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, and `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` (steps 345-346). The Optimization fit wrappers are generic in `'Parameters` (`MuellerFitting.fs`, step 337) and name no record. No alias, re-export or second declaration remains (ELEV014), so `git grep -n -E "type (UniaxialParameters|TriclinicParameters|AbsorbingTriclinicParameters) =" -- Berreman/` finds only `CrystalPhysics.fs`. The edits also name `Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`, the paths the repository census still gives the two files steps 345-346 moved; nothing is written there. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the builders and the axes are the same expressions, and no BerremanTests fact is added or removed. `LangasiteInverseTests` (the uniaxial builder and axes), `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (about 104 s, the triclinic ones) and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` (about 177 s, the absorbing ones) are the cheapest classes that drive each moved record. (4) Test, in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs`, which reaches the records from the module ahead of the material library: `{F_BUILDERS}`: over test-local records written as literals, the uniaxial record's `opticalProperties.eps` is diagonal (n_o², n_o², n_e²), the triclinic record's is diagonal (n₁², n₂², n₃²), and the absorbing record's has ε₁₁ = n₁² + i·ε″₁₁ and ε₁₂ = i·ε″₁₂ (steps 332-334's builders), each within 1e-15.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `UniaxialParameters`, `TriclinicParameters` and `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters` with their `opticalProperties` MUST be declared only in `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs`, compiled directly after `DispersionModels.fs`, and their `axes` MUST stay static members declared in `MuellerInverse.fs`; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, `BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests`, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` and `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, their numbers and counts unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `each crystal record's builder composes its permittivity from its own fields`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.
